# Hippo memory

This project uses hippo. Hippo is a local memory that your coding agents share. Use its MCP tools as follows.

- At the start of a task, call `hippo_context`. If the task is about one topic, also call `hippo_recall` with a short description of that topic. Read the result before you start.
- When you learn something that is not obvious about this code, an API or a workflow, call `hippo_remember` with one or two specific sentences.
- When something fails unexpectedly, call `hippo_remember` with what failed and why, and set `error` to true. An error memory lasts twice as long.
- After the task, call `hippo_outcome`. Set `good` to true if the recalled memories helped, or to false if they were wrong or off topic.
